    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d62">

                <pb facs="0154" n="74" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg74"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wauters to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Belgium</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">New
                            York</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1901-10-20"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">October 20,
                    1901</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary of State</hi>: In the course of the
                    month of March last Count de Lichtervelde submitted to the consideration of your
                        <pb facs="0155" n="75" xml:id="pg75"/> excellency a claim of the Compagnie
                    Générale des Philippines taken up by the Government of the King with a view of
                    procuring the restitution of a line imposed on the owners of the steamship <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Belgika</hi> for a breach of the provisions regulating
                    the coasting trade in the Philippine Islands.</p>
                <p>I have been instructed to apply again to your excellency with a request that you
                    may earnestly insist that the proper authorities take the claim of the Compagnie
                    Générale des Philippines into consideration and give it a favorable reception.
                    The Government of the King is very greatly interested in obtaining a favorable
                    solution of the matter.</p>
                <p>I should be very grateful to your excellency if you would be pleased to support
                    with your recommendation the request that I have been directed to renew. The
                    Government of the King is very desirous of having this claim entertained and of
                    securing the restitution of the tine imposed on the Belgian company, of whose
                    good faith it is satisfied.</p>
                <p>I embrace, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wauters.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
